  "body": "### Finding Description and Impact\n\nThe `validatePrice()` function in `UniswapPriceOracle.sol` is intended to compute a TWAP and reject transactions where the current price deviates too much from the time-weighted average. However, the TWAP formula self-cancels, always yielding the current spot price. This makes the oracle check completely useless as price manipulation protection.\n\n### **Root Cause**\n\n```solidity\n// L79\nuint256 cumulativePrice = cumulativePriceLast + (tradePrice * elapsedTime);\n\n// L82\nuint256 timeWeightedAverage = (cumulativePrice - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime;\n```\n\nAlgebraic simplification:\n\n```\nTWA = (cumulativePriceLast + tradePrice * elapsedTime - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime\n    = (tradePrice * elapsedTime) / elapsedTime\n    = tradePrice\n```\n\nThe `cumulativePriceLast` is added and then subtracted, cancelling entirely. The TWAP always equals the current spot price (`tradePrice`), so the derivation at L86-88 is always 0.\n\n### Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nUse the actual on-chain cumulative price from the Uniswap V2 pair instead of reconstructing it:\n\n```diff\nfunction validatePrice(uint256 slippage) external view returns (bool) {\n    require(slippage <= maxSlippage, \"Slippage overflow\");\n\n    uint256 cumulativePriceLast;\n    if (direction == 0) {\n        cumulativePriceLast = IUniswapV2(pair).price1CumulativeLast();\n    } else {\n        cumulativePriceLast = IUniswapV2(pair).price0CumulativeLast();\n    }\n\n    (, , uint256 blockTimestampLast) = IUniswapV2(pair).getReserves();\n    if (block.timestamp == blockTimestampLast) return false;\n    uint256 elapsedTime = block.timestamp - blockTimestampLast;\n\n    uint256 tradePrice = getPrice();\n\n-   uint256 cumulativePrice = cumulativePriceLast + (tradePrice * elapsedTime);\n-   uint256 timeWeightedAverage = (cumulativePrice - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime;\n+   // Use the actual on-chain cumulative price mechanism\n+   // The current cumulative price = cumulativePriceLast + (currentPrice * elapsedSinceLastUpdate)\n+   // Compare against a stored reference instead of computing a self-cancelling formula\n+   uint256 timeWeightedAverage = cumulativePriceLast / (block.timestamp - /* deployment or reference time */);\n\n    uint256 derivation = (tradePrice > timeWeightedAverage)\n        ? ((tradePrice - timeWeightedAverage) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage\n        : ((timeWeightedAverage - tradePrice) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage;\n\n    return derivation <= slippage;\n}\n```\n\nNote: The proper fix requires storing a reference cumulative price and timestamp from a previous observation, then computing the actual TWAP as `(currentCumulative - storedCumulative) / (currentTime - storedTime)`. This requires maintaining state across calls.",
